    {
      "@id": "claim:candidate-contribution-synthesis",
      "@type": "Claim",
      "label": "The candidate contribution is a bounded synthesis",
      "statement": "After a bounded primary-source review, the candidate contribution is not any component separately. It is a proposed work-centred, domain-independent semantic-artifact specification and self-demonstrating publication method that jointly: treats governed heterogeneous knowledge and process as the canonical property of a represented work rather than as agent memory or document metadata; preserves sources, assertions, interpretations, gaps, and non-erasing semantic and contribution history; exposes governed query, update, handover, and federation for people and agents; and binds human-readable or executable derivatives to traceable snapshots and lifecycles. The current semantic self-representation demonstrates structural integration and self-projection only. It does not establish global novelty, superiority, semantic completeness, cross-platform interoperability, or adoption.",
