      "@type": "Risk",
      "label": "Semantic-first workspaces concentrate integration and governance risk",
      "statement": "Combining correspondence, market data, code, demands, experiments, policies, and personal or organisational knowledge can amplify privacy leakage, access mistakes, stale or contradictory data, surveillance, authority capture, licensing conflicts, and false confidence unless source boundaries, permissions, retention, temporal validity, and accountable decisions are enforced.",
