      "@id": "source:author-clarification-team-collaboration",
      "@type": "Source",
      "label": "Author clarification: human collaboration through semantic artifacts",
      "statement": "Saeid Mokaram explained that individuals and teams can maintain semantic artifacts for their own research, development, requirements, client knowledge, product design, and other work. Rather than repeatedly translating this knowledge through meetings, documents, and prompts, an agent can use the participating artifacts together to generate proposals, APIs, product or engineering designs, CAD artifacts, code, or other solutions with fuller exposure of the available knowledge.",
