      "statement": "Saeid Mokaram defined the knowledge outcome as the available captured entirety of a work journey: raw information and data, experiment setup and results, code, tool output, observations, relations, trials, errors, discussions, conclusions, and higher-level derivations. Material can remain partially interpreted for later exploration; source facts and attributed perspectives coexist; later people or systems may add views; and anything absent must remain explicitly missing rather than being silently synthesised.",
