      "label": "Knowledge maturity continuum",
      "statement": "A non-exclusive continuum on which captured material may remain raw data or source evidence, become organised information, support observations and factual assertions, or develop into interpretations, conclusions, decisions, and higher-order judgement. The stages may coexist and need not form a universal linear hierarchy; provenance and derivation links show how a higher-level item relates to lower-level material.",
