    {
      "@id": "claim:explicit-gaps-no-synthetic-repair",
      "@type": "Claim",
      "label": "Missing knowledge must remain explicit rather than silently repaired",
      "statement": "If data, an observation, a relationship, an intermediate step, or a conclusion was not captured, the artifact and its reader agents must preserve that absence. An agent may offer a clearly labelled derivation or external context based on identified inputs, but it must not invent or silently synthesise missing material to create a complete narrative.",
