    {
      "@id": "claim:output-feedback-requires-explicit-incorporation",
      "@type": "Claim",
      "label": "Output feedback enters canonical knowledge only through an explicit event",
      "statement": "A projection or derivative does not automatically become canonical knowledge merely because it was generated or used. Corrections, results, observations, failures, user feedback, code changes, test outcomes, and newly discovered implications arising from the output may enter the knowledge source as identified evidence, proposals, decisions, or revisions only through an attributed, time-stamped, policy-governed incorporation event with links to the output and its original dependencies.",
