      "@type": "Claim",
      "label": "AI can expand the practical frontier of knowledge capture",
      "statement": "Agentic systems can reduce the effort required to collect, structure, connect, index, retrieve, compare, and project heterogeneous records while work is occurring. This may make it practical to retain substantially more first-hand evidence, process history, failed attempts, discussion, and context than workflows organised around manually authored final documents. Greater capture remains selective, fallible, governed, and empirically unproven; it is not a completeness guarantee.",
