    {
      "@id": "claim:reader-reinspection-beyond-author-narrative",
      "@type": "Claim",
      "label": "Readers can re-inspect a work beneath its final authorial narrative",
      "statement": "When source records, asserted facts, relations, and attributed interpretations remain distinguishable, later people or systems need not receive only the authors' final selection and narrative. They can inspect the represented underlying material, trace how conclusions were reached, identify gaps or contested links, compare the authors' view with the record, and add new attributed interpretations or derivations. They remain limited by capture choices, access, representation quality, and the fact that observations and asserted facts may themselves be mediated or disputed.",
