    {
      "@id": "claim:semantic-artifact-as-new-knowledge-medium",
      "@type": "Claim",
      "label": "Semantic artifacts are proposed as a candidate new knowledge medium",
      "statement": "At its broadest scale, the work proposes a historical transition from knowledge primarily handed down through author-selected, fixed representations toward governed, evolving, source-linked and queryable semantic artifacts that retain more of the recorded path from evidence and experience to interpretation and judgement. Documents remain essential projections, but they are no longer the only or canonical boundary of the represented knowledge. Calling this a fundamental shift in humanity's knowledge medium states the proposal's ambition and possible significance, not a demonstrated historical outcome or a claim that earlier cultures never preserved sources, archives, data, debate, or process.",
