    {
      "@id": "claim:semantic-collaboration-interface-shift",
      "@type": "Claim",
      "label": "Shared semantic artifacts can change the collaboration interface among people and machines",
      "statement": "At team and organisational scales, collaboration can move from repeated explanation, document exchange, individual reinterpretation, and manual agent priming toward governed exchange and federation of inspectable semantic artifacts. People and machines can work from linked requirements, evidence, constraints, experience, alternatives, and decisions while retaining source identity, authority, disagreement, and gaps. This is proposed as a structural change in the interface of collaboration, not merely faster document production and not a guarantee that communication loss disappears.",
