    {
      "@id": "evidence:agent-memory-precedent",
      "@type": "Evidence",
      "label": "Persistent agent memory, experience records, reflection, and retrieval are established precedents",
      "statement": "MemGPT demonstrates hierarchical memory management for long-context agents. Generative Agents records experience streams, synthesises reflections, and dynamically retrieves them for behaviour and planning. Persistent memory, complete recorded experience streams within an application, reflection, and retrieval are therefore not individually novel. The relevant distinction proposed here is that the governed memory belongs to a represented work, remains portable across agents and readers, and preserves source, authority, history, and derivative boundaries.",
