    {
      "@id": "argument:primary-source-novelty-boundary",
      "@type": "Argument",
      "label": "The defensible v0.1 contribution is the bounded work-centred synthesis",
      "statement": "The reviewed sources cover almost every proposed mechanism separately and sometimes in substantial combinations. The defensible v0.1 framing is therefore not that semantic structure, provenance, design rationale, automatic capture, research-object packaging, machine-readable claims, agent memory, event history, digital threads, generated human views, or agent interoperability is new. The candidate contribution is their explicit integration around the represented work as the governed canonical knowledge object, together with source-versus-interpretation boundaries, non-erasing semantic and contribution history, cross-agent query and update, federated collaboration, traceable derivative lifecycles, and a self-demonstrating publication whose paper is generated from that source. Absence of an identical system in this bounded review is not proof of global novelty.",
