    {
      "@id": "claim:machine-consumption-weakens-document-intermediation",
      "@type": "Claim",
      "label": "Machine consumption weakens the need for human-shaped documents as the primary interchange layer",
      "statement": "When a recipient already delegates repository reading, requirement interpretation or context recovery to an agentic system, a conventional human-shaped document often operates as an indirect machine interface between two bodies of work. Providing a portable semantic artifact can make that interchange more direct, structured, traceable and queryable, while preserving human-readable documents as deliberate views for comprehension, coordination, citation, narrative and accountability. The proposal is to remove mandatory document intermediation, not to remove documents or people.",
