      "@id": "concept:interactive-knowledge-dialogue",
      "@type": "Concept",
      "label": "Interactive knowledge dialogue",
      "statement": "A human or authorised agent explores a semantic artifact through a continuing question-and-answer interaction that retrieves the relevant represented sources, assertions, relations, decisions, disagreement, history and gaps. The experience can resemble questioning a knowledgeable collaborator because explanations adapt to the question and follow-up, but the interface speaks from the governed artifact rather than impersonating its contributors and cannot know tacit, inaccessible, excluded or uncaptured material.",
      "status": "working-thesis",
      "review_status": "author-reviewed",
