    {
      "@id": "claim:semantic-artifacts-may-flatten-organisational-coordination",
      "@type": "Claim",
      "label": "Semantic artifacts may flatten some organisational coordination",
      "statement": "If people and teams can expose governed knowledge directly, interrogate other teams' artifacts, and resolve explicit gaps without repeatedly relaying context through documents, meetings and managerial chains, some coordination can become more direct and less hierarchical. The proposed effect is fewer routine handovers, restatements and information-brokering layers, not the elimination of management, expert judgement, negotiation, responsibility or human contact. Its magnitude and organisational consequences remain to be evaluated.",
