    {
      "@id": "counterargument:collaboration-exceeds-information-transfer",
      "@type": "Argument",
      "label": "Collaboration is more than information transfer",
      "statement": "Meetings, conversations, management and direct human interaction do more than relay facts: they can create shared interpretation, negotiate goals and values, establish trust and accountability, surface tacit cues, resolve conflict, coordinate timing and generate new knowledge. A semantic artifact may reduce repetitive information brokerage while still weakening collaboration if it displaces these functions, gives incomplete records false authority or obscures whose judgement and responsibility are required.",
