      "@id": "question:semantic-collaboration-organisational-evaluation",
      "@type": "Question",
      "label": "When does semantic-first collaboration improve or damage organisational coordination?",
      "statement": "Compared with existing document-, meeting- and manager-mediated workflows, under which tasks and governance conditions does semantic-first collaboration reduce meeting time, handover delay, translation error, repeated agent priming and unresolved gaps while preserving or improving decision quality, shared understanding, trust, inclusion, accountability, conflict resolution, innovation and safety? Evaluation should also measure capture and maintenance burden, false confidence in completeness, power shifts, surveillance risk and failures requiring direct human coordination.",
