    {
      "@id": "example:six-week-feature-management",
      "@type": "Example",
      "label": "Six-week feature-delivery management decision",
      "statement": "A product team requests a feature within six weeks. The participating semantic artifacts connect the customer need and evidence, strategic or revenue importance, architecture and security constraints, team capacity, earlier experiments and failed implementations, external dependencies, operational risks, unanswered questions, completion criteria and approval authority. A manager asks for feasible options under the time constraint. An authorised agent returns a traceable complete-feature option dependent on an unresolved API change, a narrower lower-risk option and a temporary operational option, together with evidence, assumptions, responsible decision-makers and explicit gaps. The manager or other declared authority makes the decision and its rationale and later outcome return through governed events.",
      "status": "illustrative",
      "review_status": "author-reviewed",
      "origin": "human",
      "evidence_level": "illustrative",
