    {
      "@id": "question:technology-team-management-evaluation",
      "@type": "Question",
      "label": "Does semantic-first technology-team management improve outcomes without damaging the team?",
      "statement": "Compared with current technology-team practices, does the application reduce meeting and status-reporting time, decision latency, onboarding time, repeated questions, handover errors, unresolved gaps and context reconstruction while improving decision traceability, delivery outcomes and risk response? Evaluation must also test capture and review burden, privacy, perceived surveillance, psychological safety, trust, inclusion, contestability, management quality, learning and whether activity records are misused as performance measures.",
