      "@id": "source:author-clarification-cross-artifact-linking-and-toolkit",
      "@type": "Source",
      "label": "Author clarification: semantic linking, selective extraction and deterministic tools",
      "statement": "Saeid Mokaram proposed that semantic objects in one artifact should be able to refer to objects in another artifact during development or analysis; that a self-contained result should preserve actively linked semantics and omit unrelated source material without altering the sources; and that framework toolkits should provide deterministic operations so common processing is less dependent on agent interpretation. He asked that established knowledge-graph and semantic-graph methods be adopted where appropriate rather than reinvented.",
