      "@id": "source:author-clarification-minimal-public-semantic-package",
      "@type": "Source",
      "label": "Author clarification: the public semantic artifact should replace supporting-document proliferation",
      "statement": "Saeid Mokaram clarified that a repository intended to share a Semantic Artifact should expose the artifact itself rather than surround it with research notes, release checklists, publication plans, generated views and repeated documentation. README.md and AGENTS.md may remain as short access adapters, while the manifest, canonical knowledge and append-only history carry the meaning. Application repositories such as the Explorer retain only the code, tests and configuration necessary for that application plus their own semantic artifact. Tools, explorers, research authoring material and publication outputs remain separate linked artifacts, releases or repositories.",
