    {
      "@id": "concept:semantic-artifact-directory-package",
      "@type": "Concept",
      "label": "Semantic Artifact Directory Package",
      "statement": "A strict attached distribution of one Semantic Artifact as a visible directory whose work-specific name ends in .sa and whose root contains semantic-artifact.jsonld, knowledge.jsonld and history.jsonld with those exact role names. The manifest is the package marker and declares identity, release, governance, profile, components and optional supporting resources; filenames enable deterministic discovery while content types and structure prevent misclassification. Additional declared resources may be present without becoming canonical merely through inclusion. Tools may offer a separate content-aware import path for renamed loose files and then generate a normalised .sa package. For download or transfer, the directory may be losslessly serialized as <work-name>.sa.zip; a distribution descriptor and checksum may identify and verify that transport copy without becoming canonical content. The directory profile packages a Semantic Artifact but does not define its technology-neutral meaning or replace its manifest identity.",
      "status": "accepted",
      "review_status": "author-reviewed",
      "origin": "human",
      "evidence_level": "direct-source",
