      "@id": "source:author-proposal-document-equivalent-and-token-efficiency-metrics",
      "@type": "Source",
      "label": "Author proposal: compare a Semantic Artifact with its document-equivalent and agentic token cost",
      "statement": "Saeid Mokaram proposed evaluating, for a given Semantic Artifact, how large a conventional document or document set would need to be to capture the same represented information, and how many model or agent tokens could be saved by using the Semantic Artifact instead. The proposed experiment is especially relevant when agent-mediated work becomes a common way of consuming and applying knowledge. The purpose is to introduce measurable evidence for claimed Semantic Artifact benefits rather than rely only on conceptual arguments.",
