    {
      "@id": "risk:token-efficiency-metric-gaming",
      "@type": "Risk",
      "label": "Token-efficiency metrics can reward information loss or unfair accounting",
      "statement": "A token-saving benchmark can be made artificially favourable by omitting difficult semantic units, lowering fidelity thresholds, comparing a retrieved Semantic Artifact context with an unnecessarily verbose document, excluding Semantic Artifact construction or retrieval overhead, ignoring cached-token treatment, or counting only successful tasks. Compression can also remove qualifications, disagreement, provenance, history or source form that the framework exists to preserve. Results therefore require a shared semantic inventory, comparable conditions, explicit accounting boundaries, quality gates, negative results and independent or blinded validation where practical.",
