    {
      "@id": "instruction:prefer-current-semantic-artifact-terminology",
      "@type": "Instruction",
      "label": "Prefer the current Semantic Artifact terminology",
      "statement": "When describing current Framework meaning, use Semantic Artifact (SA) for the identified governed representation; Semantic Artifact Framework (SAF) for the generic method and evolving proposed specification; canonical semantic state for the governance-designated current representation; append-only contribution and semantic-change history for the non-erasing event record; Semantic Artifact Directory Package for the current attached .sa exchange profile; projection for a purpose-, task-, goal-, context- or audience-specific presentation; derivative for an output whose executable, operational or consequential role goes beyond presentation; Semantic Artifact Explorer (SAE) for the optional view-only application; and Semantic Artifact Toolkit for optional deterministic operations. Use work for the represented subject, which need not be a project. Treat knowledge graph, RDF, JSON-LD, Git and directories as implementation or exchange choices. Preserve project cognition, canonical knowledge base, semantic work package, starter standard, five-file bootstrap and POC only when explaining historical evolution or stable legacy identifiers; do not present them as the current preferred terms. Use hasProjection from a represented work to an output and isProjectionOf from a projection to its source; use produces for an operation's output and the British spelling specialises in current relations.",
      "status": "accepted",
      "review_status": "author-reviewed",
